{
  "tutorial": {
    "id": 4258,
    "version": 2,
    "type": "course",
    "isNew": false,
    "codeLanguage": "javascript",
    "title": "Creating Variables",
    "descriptionContent": "Learn how to create variables in JavaScript.",
    "shortDescriptionContent": "",
    "showInTrack": true,
    "iconBanner": null,
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": 17154,
        "title": "Variable Names",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145108,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Welcome to <strong>JavaScript</strong>, a versatile coding language for games.</p><p>We'll take an in-depth look into JavaScript, a <strong>programming</strong><strong>language</strong> that can power game logic, animations, and interactions.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145109,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Games need to remember things like player health, score, and position. For that, JavaScript has <strong>variables</strong>.</p><p>Like item slots, variables store values and have names that tell us what they hold.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145110,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We use <code>const</code> to create a variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" myVariable\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"set\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145111,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Every variable needs a <strong>name</strong>. Variable names need to be single words and, therefore, have no spaces.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player score\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"9\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>score</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145112,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To create variable names with multiple words, we use <strong>camel case</strong>. We start with a lowercase letter and capitalize the additional words.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player health\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerHealth\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>playerHealth</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145113,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To help us understand what's inside a variable, we pick descriptive names.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"eS\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"16\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemySpeed\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemySpeed</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145114,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's wrong with this variable name?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player Health\" /></content></code><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It contains a space</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It contains a capital letter</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It contains a space.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145115,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why do we give variables descriptive names like <code>playerHealth</code> or <code>score</code> instead of <code>x</code> or <code>y</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To help us understand what's inside them</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To make them faster to type</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To help us understand what's inside them.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145116,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What words can we use to declare variables?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>let</code> and <code>const</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>let</code> and <code>variable</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>let</code> and <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145117,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we use camel case for?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To create variable names with multiple words</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To create variable names with spaces</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To create variable names with multiple words.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145118,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Pick the most descriptive variable name.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"phs\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"21\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerHighScore\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>playerHighScore</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145119,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Spell out the word for one of the ways we use to create a variable.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"1\" endIndex=\"2\" /><option startIndex=\"2\" endIndex=\"3\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>l</code>, followed by <code>e</code>, and finally <code>t</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145120,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Put the snippets in the right order to create a variable name.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /><option startIndex=\"4\" endIndex=\"15\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerScore\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>let</code>, followed by <code>playerScore</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 145121,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Finish up creating this variable by coding <code>let</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" player}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>let</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17155,
        "title": "Variable Values",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145122,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variable names can contain <strong>numbers</strong>, too. Adding numbers is useful with multiple similar variables. Let's create the variable <code>enemy1</code> here.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"1 enemy\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"12\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemy1\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemy1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145123,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>After creating and naming a variable, we use the <code>=</code> sign to store a <strong>value</strong> inside it. Like <code>const levelName = \"Forest\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>\"Forest\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145124,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To finish creating a variable, we put a semicolon, <code>;</code>, at the end of the line.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\".\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145125,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The values we've been storing like <code>\"Forest\"</code> are <strong>strings</strong>. Strings are words in double quotes.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"&quot;Forest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"</code>, followed by <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145126,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Strings can contain all sorts of letters and symbols, including spaces. For example, <code>\"Game Over\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"1\" /><option startIndex=\"1\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"11\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"&quot;Game Over&quot;\" class=\"string\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"</code>, followed by <code>Game Over</code>, and finally <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145127,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the value of this variable?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Karin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>\"Karin\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>playerName</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"Karin\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145128,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we know a value is a string?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">It's a word between double quotes</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">It contains an <code>=</code> sign</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It's a word between double quotes.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145129,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's happening in this code?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameState = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Playing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The variable <code>gameState</code> stores the value <code>\"Playing\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The variable <code>\"Playing\"</code> stores the value <code>gameState</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The variable <code>gameState</code> stores the value <code>\"Playing\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145130,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the name of this variable?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" weapon = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Tree shaping&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>weapon</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"Tree shaping\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>weapon</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145131,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create a <code>playerClass</code> variable and give it the value <code>\"Plumber\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"41\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"53\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mario&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerClass = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Plumber&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>let playerClass</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>\"Plumber\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145132,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create a <code>studio</code> variable and give it a string value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"Apple\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"21\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" studio = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Apple&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>let studio</code> followed by <code>=</code> and then <code>\"Apple\"</code>, <code>;</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145133,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Give the <code>spawnPoint</code> variable a string value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"'\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" spawnPoint = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Malta&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"</code>, followed by <code>Malta</code>, and finally <code>\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145134,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Give the <code>platform</code> variable the string value <code>\"Desktop\"</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"17\" endIndex=\"26\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" platform = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Desktop&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>\"Desktop\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17156,
        "title": "Let and Const Differences",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145135,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We already know we can declare variables with <code>let</code> and <code>const</code>. Let's find out the difference between them in a game!</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145136,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We use <code>const</code> to declare values that should not change during the game. <code>const</code> is short for \"constant\".</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" STARTING_LEVEL = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>, followed by <code>STARTING_LEVEL</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145137,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>If we try to update a value stored in a <code>const</code> variable, we will get an error.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"120\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145138,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>However, we can update <code>let</code> variables with the assign <code>=</code> operator.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"const\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"score = \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>let</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145139,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To make it obvious that a variable is of type <code>const</code> and shouldn't change, we can optionally name it with uppercase letters.</p><p>Create an uppercase <code>spawn point</code> constant.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"spawnPoint\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"spawn_point\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"17\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" SPAWN_POINT = \" /><text value=\"&quot;TownGate&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>SPAWN_POINT</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145140,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We cannot use <code>camelCase</code> if we use this uppercase standard, so we use an uppercase <code>snake_case</code> to name variables with more than one word.</p><p>Create an <em>uppercase</em> \"player max health\" const using <code>snake_case</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"player_max_health\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"playerMaxHealth\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"23\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" PLAYER_MAX_HEALTH = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>PLAYER_MAX_HEALTH</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145141,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Both <code>let</code> and <code>const</code> are useful variables and we could use them interchangeably. However, we should try to use <code>const</code> as the default.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"let\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" GAME_TITLE = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sprite Quest&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145142,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does <code>const</code> stand for?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">constant</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">continuous</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick constant.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145143,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can assign a new value to a <code>let</code> variable.</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">true</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">false</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick true.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145144,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the optional standard to make sure constants don't change their values?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">uppercase</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">lowercase snake case</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick uppercase.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145145,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What should we use as a default?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>const</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>let</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145146,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Declare the variable correctly.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"3\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" currentLevel = \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"currentLevel = \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>let</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145147,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use the uppercase <code>snake_case</code> standard to declare this <code>const</code> variable.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"final_boss_name\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"FINALBOSSNAME\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"21\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" FINAL_BOSS_NAME = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Hydra&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>FINAL_BOSS_NAME</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 145148,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use the default variable to declare the game name.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" GAME_NAME = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Dungeon Dash&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>const</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 17157,
        "title": "Console",
        "type": "practiceLevel1",
        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 145149,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Lines of code are <strong>instructions</strong> for a game to follow.</p><p>When we run code, we tell the game to follow the instructions we put together.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 145150,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The order of the instructions matters because the game follows them line by line.</p><p>Create <code>step1</code> first, <code>step2</code> second, and <code>step3</code> third.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"29\" /><option startIndex=\"30\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"89\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" step1 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Spawn player&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" step2 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Start game loop&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" step3 = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Win level&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const step1 = \"Spawn player\";</code>, followed by <code>const step2 = \"Start game loop\";</code>, and finally <code>const step3 = \"Win level\";</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 145151,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>With the special instruction <code>console.log()</code>, we tell the computer to display a value in an area called the <strong>console</strong>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"12\" endIndex=\"27\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Game started!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"Game started!\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 145152,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use the <code>console.log()</code> instruction as often as we want. The computer displays every value on a line in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option startIndex=\"50\" endIndex=\"51\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Loading level...&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;GO!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>(</code>, followed by <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 145153,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can use <code>console.log()</code> to display variables like <code>playerState</code>, too.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"console.log\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\")\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"40\" endIndex=\"51\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerState = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Idle&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerState);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>playerState</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 145154,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we display variables in the console, their values appear instead of their names. If we log <code>enemyName</code> here, it'll show its value.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"39\" endIndex=\"48\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyName);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>enemyName</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 145155,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How do we know <code>\"Game started!\"</code> is a string?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">It starts and ends with double quotes</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">It contains letters and symbols</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It starts and ends with double quotes.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 145156,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the console?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">An area that displays output</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">The area where we write the code</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">An area that displays output.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 145157,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does the special instruction <code>console.log()</code> do?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">It displays a value in the console</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">It creates a variable</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It displays a value in the console.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 145158,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display in the console?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" levelName = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Dungeon 1&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(levelName);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>Dungeon 1</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>levelName</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>Dungeon 1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 145159,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Put the code in order to display the value <code>100</code> in the console.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"52\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerHealth = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerHealth);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>const playerHealth = 100;</code>, followed by <code>console.log(playerHealth);</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 145160,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add the instruction to display this string value in the console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"7\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"8\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"23\" endIndex=\"24\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Level up!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>console</code> followed by <code>.</code> and then <code>log</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 145161,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Display the value of <code>score</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"4200\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"32\" endIndex=\"37\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" score = \" /><text value=\"4200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(score);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>score</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 145162,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Display the value of the <code>gameState</code> variable.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"41\" endIndex=\"50\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" gameState = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Playing&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(gameState);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>gameState</code>.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
